From: Antminer S19K Pro bring-up, github.com/tronsington/mujina
Subject: [PATCH] S19K Pro: Core byte order, NonceRange revert, bit-bang PSU

PROVENANCE
==========

This patch modifies code belonging to another project. It is NOT a
patch against this repository.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/Schnitzel/mujina
  Branch:    amlogic-s19kpro-support
  Applies to: 9837ef71a6e82639e336830ddeae5cb530965eb9
              ("S19k Pro Amlogic: bring up all present hashboards in
               parallel")
  Licence:   GPL-3.0-or-later, the same as this repository, so it is
             redistributable here with attribution.

  To use it:
      git clone --branch amlogic-s19kpro-support --single-branch \
          https://github.com/Schnitzel/mujina.git schnitzel-mujina
      cd schnitzel-mujina
      git checkout 9837ef7
      git apply /path/to/s19k-fixes.patch

WHAT IT CHANGES, AND WHOSE WORK IT IS
=====================================

The surrounding S19K Pro port --- the board driver, the chip config
table, the bring-up sequencing --- is Schnitzel's work. This patch is
five files of changes on top of it:

  chip_config.rs   BM1366's `Core` (0x3C, CORE_MAILBOX) values were
                   stored byte-reversed, so the chips received bit 31
                   clear and "apply to all cores" never took effect.
                   Stored big-endian now, matching bm1362()/bm1370().
                   The guarding unit test asserted the wrong byte order
                   and is corrected too --- which is why CI stayed green
                   over the bug.
  sequencer.rs     revert NonceRange to the captured BM1366 value
  board/mod.rs     wire up the PSU shim below
  psu_bitbang_i2c.rs (new)
                   this unit's PSU is not reachable through any
                   /dev/i2c-N device --- it answers only on bit-banged
                   GPIO 476/477. Without this the port cannot power the
                   board at all.
  s19k_pro_amlogic.rs
                   use the shim, and default fans to 100%

Applying it took that fork from ~2.9 TH/s to ~105 TH/s on real
hardware, verified against the pool's own accounting. Full analysis:
docs/s19k-pro/root-cause.md. Licensing detail: docs/s19k-pro/ATTRIBUTION.md.

Note that `chip_config.rs` exists only in that fork; neither this
repository nor upstream 256foundation/mujina has that file, so this is
their bug and their fix, not an upstream one.

---
